course: dictionary
lesson: 12054
title: Clad: dressed or covered
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Clad is an old-fashioned word that means wearing something or covered by something. You will often find it in stories and poems. «The knight was clad in shining armour.» The armour covers the knight, so clad means dressed or covered in something.
explain: Clad often comes with «in», as in «clad in». The words around it are the clues. «A tall figure clad in black stood by the door.» The words «in black» tell you what the figure is wearing, so clad must be about clothes.
explain: Clad can also describe a surface that has a layer over it. «The old stone cottage was clad in ivy.» The ivy is a layer covering the walls. Builders also use the verb clad: «Workers clad the school walls with new wooden panels» means they covered the walls with a layer of material.
fact: Clad means wearing certain clothes, or covered with a layer of some material.
fact: «Clad» is often used in stories, poems and the news, not in everyday talk.
fact: Clad often goes with «in», as in «clad in».
fact: Cladding is the layer of material that covers the outside of a building.
fact: To clad a wall means to cover it with a layer of material.
exercise: «The knight was clad in shining armour.» What does clad mean here? | Painted bright red | Carrying a sword | *Wearing or covered by | Running away from
exercise: «The old stone cottage was clad in ivy.» What does clad suggest about the ivy? | It is cooking dinner inside | *It covers the walls like a layer | It has cut through the roof | It is lost in the forest
exercise: «A tall figure clad in black stood by the door.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the figure was dressed. | *clad | door | stood | figure
test: «Workers clad the school walls with new wooden panels.» What does clad mean here? | To clean the windows | *To cover with a layer of material | To paint the walls green | To knock the walls down
test: What is cladding on a building? | The bell at the top of a school | A hat worn by builders | The path to the front door | *The layer of material that covers the walls
exam: Which word means covered with a layer, as in «ivy-clad»? | Empty | Shiny | Bare | *Clad
